    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-c3pb6844ll78",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 828,
      "width": 648.0,
      "height": 54,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-11: knowledge tenancy gains the reserved `_shared` read-only partition\n(public legal corpus consulted by every org search; org-private uploads stay isolated;\nno real actor ever carries the '_shared' org id - writes through the service are refused).",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-11: knowledge tenancy gains the reserved `_shared` read-only partition\n(public legal corpus consulted by every org search; org-private uploads stay isolated;\nno real actor ever carries the '_shared' org id - writes through the service are refused).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 616930969,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 94830821,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-11: knowledge tenancy gains the reserved `_shared` read-only partition\n(public legal corpus consulted by every org search; org-private uploads stay isolated;\nno real actor ever carries the '_shared' org id - writes through the service are refused)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "s4a-tenancy-note",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 906,
      "width": 740,
      "height": 120.0,
      "text": "S4a 2026-07-17: gateway_keys rows carry ownerUserId + orgId. Keys are OWNER-scoped (mint/list/\nrevoke only by owner; cross-user revoke = uniform 404). A key turn bills the owner and rate-caps\ncompose per key -> per user -> per org; the gateway_turn Registo row is org-stamped for the\norg-admin Registo read surface.",
      "originalText": "S4a 2026-07-17: gateway_keys rows carry ownerUserId + orgId. Keys are OWNER-scoped (mint/list/\nrevoke only by owner; cross-user revoke = uniform 404). A key turn bills the owner and rate-caps\ncompose per key -> per user -> per org; the gateway_turn Registo row is org-stamped for the\norg-admin Registo read surface.",
      "fontSize": 24,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 74747490,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 74747491,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "updated": 1784282275492
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-memvault-e2-a2ea5910",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 1056.0,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 140.0,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-30 (memvault, slice E2): memvault tenancy is PER USER, stricter than org scoping - each\nuser's notes live under <memvault root>/<userId>/ and no request can address another partition: the\npermalink grammar (no dots, no absolute, max 512) makes traversal unrepresentable, and jail.ts\nrealpath-containment-checks the deepest existing ancestor so a pre-planted symlink into another user's\ntree (or /etc) fails CLOSED. On the wire, missing / cross-tenant / jail-refused are ONE uniform 404 (the\nscoped.ts no-oracle discipline); the difference lands only in the audit trail (verdict jail_violation).\nBoth admissions of 'user-or-key' (platform JWT, ekoa_gk_ key) resolve to the SAME owner partition;\nisolation suite: api/tests/security/memvault-isolation.test.ts.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-30 (memvault, slice E2): memvault tenancy is PER USER, stricter than org scoping - each\nuser's notes live under <memvault root>/<userId>/ and no request can address another partition: the\npermalink grammar (no dots, no absolute, max 512) makes traversal unrepresentable, and jail.ts\nrealpath-containment-checks the deepest existing ancestor so a pre-planted symlink into another user's\ntree (or /etc) fails CLOSED. On the wire, missing / cross-tenant / jail-refused are ONE uniform 404 (the\nscoped.ts no-oracle discipline); the difference lands only in the audit trail (verdict jail_violation).\nBoth admissions of 'user-or-key' (platform JWT, ekoa_gk_ key) resolve to the SAME owner partition;\nisolation suite: api/tests/security/memvault-isolation.test.ts.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 1605690162,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1522325281,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-30 (memvault, slice E2): memvault tenancy is PER USER, stricter than org scoping - each\nuser's notes live under <memvault root>/<userId>/ and no request can address another partition: the\npermalink grammar (no dots, no absolute, max 512) makes traversal unrepresentable, and jail.ts\nrealpath-containment-checks the deepest existing ancestor so a pre-planted symlink into another user's\ntree (or /etc) fails CLOSED. On the wire, missing / cross-tenant / jail-refused are ONE uniform 404 (the\nscoped.ts no-oracle discipline); the difference lands only in the audit trail (verdict jail_violation).\nBoth admissions of 'user-or-key' (platform JWT, ekoa_gk_ key) resolve to the SAME owner partition;\nisolation suite: api/tests/security/memvault-isolation.test.ts."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260803-b2-review-org-shared-credentials",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 1230,
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 980,
      "height": 122.5,
      "seed": 1,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (B2 review C1/H1) - ORG-SHARED CREDENTIALS: what crosses the owner boundary.\nA credential is owner-scoped and stays owner-scoped for READING (decisions.md 2026-07-27). But an org-shared\nintegration config is held by the whole org, so two things about its credential item are now ORG-reachable\nthrough the server-stamped join: the EGRESS BINDING (a peer gets the admin's bound origins, and [] the moment\nthe admin locks it) and DESTRUCTION (any admin who may delete the config destroys its item + grants). Both are\nrestrictions; neither is disclosure. A peer still cannot unwrap the admin's credential, and the comparator\nstill answers shadow_unreachable for them - which is exactly the question the 2026-08-15 cutover review owns.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (B2 review C1/H1) - ORG-SHARED CREDENTIALS: what crosses the owner boundary.\nA credential is owner-scoped and stays owner-scoped for READING (decisions.md 2026-07-27). But an org-shared\nintegration config is held by the whole org, so two things about its credential item are now ORG-reachable\nthrough the server-stamped join: the EGRESS BINDING (a peer gets the admin's bound origins, and [] the moment\nthe admin locks it) and DESTRUCTION (any admin who may delete the config destroys its item + grants). Both are\nrestrictions; neither is disclosure. A peer still cannot unwrap the admin's credential, and the comparator\nstill answers shadow_unreachable for them - which is exactly the question the 2026-08-15 cutover review owns.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (B2 review C1/H1) - ORG-SHARED CREDENTIALS: what crosses the owner boundary.\nA credential is owner-scoped and stays owner-scoped for READING (decisions.md 2026-07-27). But an org-shared\nintegration config is held by the whole org, so two things about its credential item are now ORG-reachable\nthrough the server-stamped join: the EGRESS BINDING (a peer gets the admin's bound origins, and [] the moment\nthe admin locks it) and DESTRUCTION (any admin who may delete the config destroys its item + grants). Both are\nrestrictions; neither is disclosure. A peer still cannot unwrap the admin's credential, and the comparator\nstill answers shadow_unreachable for them - which is exactly the question the 2026-08-15 cutover review owns.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-ws8a-shared-scope-20260808",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 1360,
      "width": 700.0,
      "height": 126,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-08 (WS8a): listCollections/listDocuments gain an additive `scope` query\nparam ('org' default, unchanged; 'shared' opt-in) so any authenticated org actor may BROWSE\n(never write) the `_shared` corpus through the same tier-1 capability surface search already\nused - closing the visibility gap search never had (a fresh org's own vault looked empty even\nthough `_shared` held 262k+ documents). The Biblioteca UI adds a scope toggle + a search box\nover the existing POST /search (already unions org + `_shared`); a `_shared` row never offers\na delete affordance client-side, mirroring the server's read-only enforcement.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-08 (WS8a): listCollections/listDocuments gain an additive `scope` query\nparam ('org' default, unchanged; 'shared' opt-in) so any authenticated org actor may BROWSE\n(never write) the `_shared` corpus through the same tier-1 capability surface search already\nused - closing the visibility gap search never had (a fresh org's own vault looked empty even\nthough `_shared` held 262k+ documents). The Biblioteca UI adds a scope toggle + a search box\nover the existing POST /search (already unions org + `_shared`); a `_shared` row never offers\na delete affordance client-side, mirroring the server's read-only enforcement.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 20260808,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 20260808,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-08 (WS8a): listCollections/listDocuments gain an additive `scope` query\nparam ('org' default, unchanged; 'shared' opt-in) so any authenticated org actor may BROWSE\n(never write) the `_shared` corpus through the same tier-1 capability surface search already\nused - closing the visibility gap search never had (a fresh org's own vault looked empty even\nthough `_shared` held 262k+ documents). The Biblioteca UI adds a scope toggle + a search box\nover the existing POST /search (already unions org + `_shared`); a `_shared` row never offers\na delete affordance client-side, mirroring the server's read-only enforcement."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "annot-grounding-gate-2026-08-13",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 1526,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 108,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-13 (grounding relevance gate - the todo-app Jurisprudencia finding):\n- the reserved `_shared` legal corpus joins a GROUNDING search only when the deterministic\n  legal-context detector matches the query (both chat and build kinds); the org's OWN partition is\n  always searched. index-store search() gains includeShared (default true - browse/portal unchanged).\n- app-assistant citations are now USED-ONLY: retrieval hits feed the prompt, but only excerpts the\n  reply referenced ([n]) are cited to the visitor (apps/app-assistant.ts usedCitations).",
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-13 (grounding relevance gate - the todo-app Jurisprudencia finding):\n- the reserved `_shared` legal corpus joins a GROUNDING search only when the deterministic\n  legal-context detector matches the query (both chat and build kinds); the org's OWN partition is\n  always searched. index-store search() gains includeShared (default true - browse/portal unchanged).\n- app-assistant citations are now USED-ONLY: retrieval hits feed the prompt, but only excerpts the\n  reply referenced ([n]) are cited to the visitor (apps/app-assistant.ts usedCitations).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
